1
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Everyone knows the icon. Few know the man.

2
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Che: Part One is a drama, history, war film directed by Steven Soderbergh.

3
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ernesto Guevara, known as 'Che', leads a group of Cuban exiles under Fidel Castro in
a revolution to overthrow Fulgencio Batista, the dictator of Cuba.

4
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Ernesto Che Guevara, played by Benicio del Toro.

5
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Fidel Castro, played by Demián Bichir.

6
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Camilo Cienfuegos, played by Santiago Cabrera.

7
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Ramiro Valdés Menéndez, played by Vladimir Cruz.

8
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Israel Pardo, played by Alfredo de Quesada.

9
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Jorge Sotus, played by Jsu Garcia.

10
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:46,000
Che is a two-part 2008 epic biographical film about the Argentine Marxist
revolutionary Ernesto "Che" Guevara, directed by Steven Soderbergh.

11
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Rather than follow a standard chronological order, the films offer an oblique
series of interspersed moments along the overall timeline.

12
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Part One is titled The Argentine and focuses on the Cuban Revolution from the landing of Fidel Castro, Guevara, and other
revolutionaries in Cuba to their successful toppling of Fulgencio Batista's dictatorship two years later.

13
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:10,000
Part Two is titled Guerrilla and focuses on Guevara's attempt
to bring revolution to Bolivia and his demise.

14
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:38,000
Both parts are shot in a cinéma vérité style, but each has different
approaches to linear narrative, camerawork and the visual look.

15
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
It stars Benicio del Toro as Guevara, with an ensemble cast that includes Demián Bichir, Rodrigo Santoro, Santiago Cabrera, Franka Potente, Julia Ormond, Vladimir Cruz,
Marc-André Grondin, Lou Diamond Phillips, Joaquim de Almeida, Édgar Ramírez, Yul Vazquez, Unax Ugalde, Alfredo De Quesada, Jordi Mollá, Matt Damon, and Oscar Isaac.

16
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
Filmmaker Terrence Malick originally worked on a screenplay limited to
Guevara's attempts to start a revolution in Bolivia.

17
01:15:56,000 --> 01:16:02,000
When financing fell through, Malick left the project, and
Soderbergh subsequently agreed to direct the film.

18
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:30,000
He realized that there was no context for Guevara's actions in Bolivia and decided that his participation in
the Cuban Revolution and his appearance at the United Nations in 1964 should also be depicted.

19
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:58,000
Peter Buchman was hired to write the screenplay — the script was so long that Soderbergh decided to
divide the film into two parts: one chronicling Cuba, the other depicting Bolivia.

20
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
Soderbergh shot the installments back-to-back starting at the beginning of July 2007, with Guerrilla
first in Spain for 39 days, and The Argentine shot in Puerto Rico and Mexico for 39 days.

21
01:33:48,000 --> 01:33:54,000
Che was screened as a single film at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival.

22
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:22,000
Del Toro won the Best Actor Award, and the film
received mostly positive reviews.

23
01:42:44,000 --> 01:42:50,000
IFC Films, which holds all North American rights, initially released the combined film for one week on 12
December 2008 in New York City and Los Angeles to qualify for the year's Academy Awards.

24
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
Strong box office performance led to the "special roadshow edition" being
extended in NYC and LA, and later expanded into additional markets.

25
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:46,000
It was released as two separate films, titled Che Part 1: The Argentine and
Che Part 2: Guerrilla, and further distribution followed.

26
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:14,000
The Independent Film Channel released the films via video on demand
and on Region 1 DVD exclusively from Blockbuster.

27
02:00:36,000 --> 02:00:42,000
As a whole, Che grossed US$40.9 million worldwide,
against a budget of US$58 million.

28
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:10,000
The film explores themes of hero, central intelligence
agency (cia), cuba, biography, che guevara.

29
02:09:32,000 --> 02:09:38,000
The tone is emotional.
